SUMMARY:Deadline: Sarabande Foundation: Studio Residency 2026/27 (UK-based 
 only)
DESCRIPTION:The Sarabande Foundation\, founded by Lee Alexander McQueen\, o
 ffers subsidised London studio residencies for creatives across discipline
 s (fine art\, fashion\, design\, digital)\, with structured mentoring and 
 pro bono expert support. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must have a UK address an
 d the right to work in the UK\; the foundation cannot sponsor visas. Deadl
 ine 1 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Sarabande Foundation\nLocation: London
 \, United Kingdom. Requires a UK address and right to work in the UK\; no 
 visa sponsorship.\nAward: Heavily subsidised studio space (GBP 1 per sq ft
  per month including utilities)\, mentoring from industry experts\, pro bo
 no business support\, and access to the Sarabande network. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: Residencies start November 2026.\n\nMore: https://sarabandefoun
 dation.org/en-us/pages/studio-residencies-scholarships?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sarabandefoundation.org/en-us/pages/studio-residencies-scholars
 hips?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:London\, United Kingdom. Requires a UK address and right to work i
 n the UK\; no visa sponsorship.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-argyll-sea-change-animated-women-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T212305Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Argyll: Sea Change - Animated Women 2026-27 (envir
 onmental animation development)
DESCRIPTION:Sea Change is a seven-month professional development programme 
 from Screen Argyll for six UK-based women and marginalised gender animator
 s developing animated feature film projects\, with environmental storytell
 ing at the centre of the brief. It runs a project from concept toward scre
 en: online workshops in early September 2026\, a residential lab on the Is
 le of Tiree from 15 to 22 September 2026\, monthly mentoring from October 
 2026 to February 2027\, a project showcase at MOVE Summit in February 2027
 \, and final submissions in March 2027. WHAT PARTICIPANTS GET: GBP 150 per
  day for 20 days of participation\, which comes to GBP 3\,000\; accommodat
 ion covered during the residential lab\; travel support\; and industry pas
 ses for MOVE Summit and Glasgow Film Festival 2027. ELIGIBILITY: UK reside
 nt\, over 18\, a woman or marginalised gender animator\, not in full-time 
 education when the programme begins\, with prior experience making short-f
 orm or longer animation\, and a feature project at early-to-mid developmen
 t stage. NOTE THE TIMING: the deadline is 10 August 2026 and selected proj
 ects are notified on 17 August 2026\, so this is a short-turnaround applic
 ation.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Argyll\nLocation: UK-based applicants. Onli
 ne workshops plus a residential lab on the Isle of Tiree\, Scotland\, and 
 a showcase at MOVE Summit\, Edinburgh.\nAward: GBP 150 per day for 20 days
  of participation (GBP 3\,000 total)\, plus covered accommodation during t
 he residential lab\, travel support\, and industry passes for MOVE Summit 
 and Glasgow Film Festival 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: Seven month
 s\, September 2026 to March 2027. Deadline 10 August 2026\; selections ann
 ounced 17 August 2026.\n\nMore: https://screenargyll.co.uk/sea-change-anim
 ated-women/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://screenargyll.co.uk/sea-change-animated-women/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK-based applicants. Online workshops plus a residential lab on th
 e Isle of Tiree\, Scotland\, and a showcase at MOVE Summit\, Edinburgh.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gasworks-residency-east-africa-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212305Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gasworks Residency 2027: Artists Based in East Africa
DESCRIPTION:Gasworks residency open call for an early-career contemporary v
 isual artist based in East Africa. The eleven-week\, fully funded residenc
 y runs at Gasworks in London from 7 April to 22 June 2027. Gasworks' resid
 ency programme supports professional development\, cultural exchange and a
 rtistic experimentation\, hosting up to twenty residencies a year\; reside
 ncies are self-led\, non-prescriptive and process-based\, with artists exp
 ected to lead on the research and production of their own work while Gaswo
 rks provides administrative\, pastoral and curatorial support during offic
 e hours. The residency includes studio visits with Gasworks staff\, extern
 al curators\, artists and educational groups\, at least two individual stu
 dio visits with other artists\, curators and arts professionals\, networki
 ng opportunities\, a dedicated residency page on the Gasworks website with
  a short video interview filmed and edited by Gasworks\, and an Open Studi
 o event and presentation of the work and research developed during the res
 idency on 12 June 2027. ELIGIBILITY: early-career contemporary visual arti
 sts based in Burundi\, the Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethio
 pia\, Eritrea\, the French Southern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Mal
 awi\, Mauritius\, Mayotte\, Mozambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, S
 omalia\, South Sudan\, Uganda\, the United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia 
 only. Applicants should have at least a moderate level of spoken English a
 nd feel comfortable discussing their work in English. The residency is off
 ered subject to approval of the visa application. Deadline 28 September 20
 26\, 12:00 UTC. No fee.\n\nOrganisation: Gasworks\nLocation: Gasworks\, Lo
 ndon\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based in East Africa: Burundi\, 
 Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethiopia\, Eritrea\, French Sout
 hern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Malawi\, Mauritius\, Mayotte\, Moz
 ambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, Somalia\, South Sudan\, Uganda\,
  United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia.\nAward: Fully funded eleven-week r
 esidency: 24/7 access to a fully accessible private studio at Gasworks\; s
 ingle-room accommodation in Gasworks' Residency House (shared two-storey h
 ouse with three communal bathrooms and a kitchen)\; economy return flights
  and taxi transfers from the artist's home country to London (one cabin an
 d one hold bag)\; all visa costs and visa-application support\; weekly sti
 pend of GBP 175 for living expenses\; materials budget of up to GBP 800\; 
 prepaid TFL Zones 1+2 travel card for unlimited central London travel thro
 ughout the residency\; access to Gasworks' basic tools and AV equipment su
 bject to availability. No application fee.\nDuration: Eleven weeks\, 7 Apr
 il to 22 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/resi
 dency-open-call-for-artists-based-in-east-africa-2027?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency-open-call-for-artis
 ts-based-in-east-africa-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Gasworks\, London\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based in Ea
 st Africa: Burundi\, Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethiopia\, 
 Eritrea\, French Southern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Malawi\, Maur
 itius\, Mayotte\, Mozambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, Somalia\, S
 outh Sudan\, Uganda\, United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia.
END:VEVENT
